<title>JAPAN: M'bishi Oct domestic output up 6.2% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>M'bishi Oct domestic output up 6.2% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsubishi Motors Corp said on Wednesday its domestic vehicle production, exports, domestic sales and overseas production in October were, with percentage change from a year earlier, as follows:</p>
<p> Production	  102,073   up  6.2 percent</p>
<p>  - Car		 68,126   up  4.2 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     33,947   up 10.5 percent</p>
<p> Domestic sales     55,795   up  8.7 percent</p>
<p>  - Car		 29,965   up  8.5 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     25,830   up  8.8 percent</p>
<p> Exports		34,012   up  5.8 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		22,244   up  6.3 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     11,768   up  4.9 percent</p>
<p> Overseas output    75,732   up 25.6 percent</p>
<p>Mitsubishi's domestic vehicle production in October rose for the second straight month on a year-on-year basis, reflecting recovering domestic sales and higher exports.</p>
<p>Its domestic sales rose for the first time in eight months, helped by strond demand for its new Galant sedans and Legnum station wagons, a Mitsubishi spokesman said.</p>
<p>Mitsubishi's exports rose for the third straight month and its overseas output rose for the fourth straight month.</p>
</text>
